  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Gu Yue Bo teaches Fang Zheng to fuse Jade Skin Gu and Moonlight Gu into rank two Moon Raiment. That pair already satisfies one of the Gu Yue clan’s rank five recipes, whose end is Moonlight Treasure King Gu, but Bo tells Fang Zheng that naming a rank five Gu is still too early and starts him on this rank two step. The first attempt fails when Fang Zheng loses the fused consciousness. Bo warns that too many failures can destroy both source Gu. After that failure the Moonlight Gu shows cracks and the Jade Skin Gu looks weakened.",
        "chapters": [
          98
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_gu_yue_bo",
          "char_fang_zheng",
          "gu_jade_skin_gu",
          "gu_moonlight_gu",
          "fac_gu_yue_clan",
          "gu_moonlight_treasure_king_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan’s later survey of Moonlight Gu routes records that Fang Zheng used Moonlight Gu and Jade Skin Gu to create Moon Raiment, a rare line whose upper limit is rank five Moonlight Treasure King Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          106
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "moonlight-routes",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Zheng’s rank two Moon Raiment already gives him the ability to fight Fang Yuan.",
        "chapters": [
          107
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "fighting-strength",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "White Jade Gu is not the Raiment Gu. White Jade Gu cannot lessen the force of an impact; Fang Yuan’s back still hurts after a fall of three to four meters.",
        "chapters": [
          150
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "impact-force",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "On the Qing Mao Mountain battlefield Fang Zheng shouts the Gu’s name and activates it. A misty light that is blue like the moon gushes from his body, extending and surrounding the Gu Masters around him.",
        "chapters": [
          190
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "group-barrier",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_qing_mao_mountain",
          "fac_gu_masters"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Inside an ice chunk, Fang Zheng’s whole body is covered with a layer of moonlight from Moon Raiment Gu. He had used it against Ironbeak flying cranes until one crane broke through the barrier and pecked his forehead, after which he lost consciousness.",
        "chapters": [
          199
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "crane-assault",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
